---
const rows = [
  ['Design', 'copy that needs another pass', 'missing sequence or context'],
  ['Product', 'onboarding friction', 'action requested too early'],
  ['Support', 'tickets that should not exist', 'product guidance moved to humans'],
  ['Engineering', 'edge cases', 'system assumptions not constrained'],
  ['Customer Success', 'repeated explanation', 'missing scaffold carried manually'],
  ['Leadership', 'activation, conversion, or data-quality risk', 'cost transfer across teams'],
];
---
<section id="recognition">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-label">Recognition</div>
    <h2>Your team may already be naming the symptom wrong.</h2>
    <div class="symptom-ledger" role="table" aria-label="Symptom ledger">
      <div class="ledger-head" role="row"><span>Team</span><span>What they call it</span><span>What may actually be happening</span></div>
      {rows.map(([team, label, diagnosis]) => <div class="ledger-row" role="row"><span>{team}</span><span>{label}</span><strong>{diagnosis}</strong></div>)}
    </div>
    <p class="section-copy">They may all be paying for the same failure from different budgets: the product asks the user to continue before the next move has been made legible.</p>
    <p class="section-copy recognition-close">That is where the review begins.</p>
  </div>
</section>
